13	// vendored records, or none — every query answers from what the mount actually
14	// holds. The full registry (engine/migrations/registry.mjs) builds on this same
15	// surface canon-side.
16	//
17	// TWO HOMES, ONE SHAPE. A record belongs to the flow that owns it: an engine
18	// migration lives at `engine/migrations/<landed-date>-<slug>/`, a pack's at
19	// `packs/<pack>/migrations/<landed-date>-<slug>/`, each with its spec at
20	// migration.mjs (docs/versioned-updates/DESIGN.md §3.7). Discovery walks both,
21	// so a caller never has to know which flow raised a record — and the split is
22	// what lets each flow fetch, and later version-range, only its own.
23	//
24	// All records are equal — there is no active/archived split and no cleanup pass;
25	// FETCHING decides relevance. Vendoring ships only the records landed within
26	// RECENT_WINDOW_DAYS, so an up-to-date consumer carries few-to-none, while a
27	// lagging project updating out of a fresh canon clone sees them all and
28	// applies what it needs.
